{"id":"NCT06991257","title":"A Study to Learn About the Study Medicine Called PF-07328948 in Adults With Heart Failure (BRANCH-HF)","official":"A PHASE 2, RANDOMIZED, DOUBLE-BLIND, PLACEBO-CONTROLLED STUDY TO EVALUATE THE EFFICACY AND SAFETY OF AN ORAL BRANCHED-CHAIN KETOACID DEHYDROGENASE KINASE INHIBITOR, PF-07328948, IN ADULTS WITH HEART FAILURE (BRANCH-HF)","summary":"The purpose of this study is to learn about the safety and effects of the study medicine (PF-07328948) for the possible treatment of heart failure (HF).","conditions":["Heart Failure"],"interventions":[{"type":"DRUG","name":"Placebo"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Low Dose PF-07328948"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Medium Dose PF-07328948"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"High Dose PF-07328948"}],"criteria":"This study is seeking participants who are:\n\nKey Inclusion Criteria include:\n\n* aged 18 years to \\< 80 years\n* clinically confirmed to have a diagnosis of heart failure for at least 3 months\n* New York Heart Association Class II-IV symptoms\n* left ventricular ejection fraction greater than 40%\n* Kansas City Cardiomyopathy Questionnaire-23 Total Symptom Score \\< 85\n* Six-minute walking distance greater than 75 meters\n\nKey Exclusion Criteria include:\n\n* Type 1 diabetes mellitus, liver cirrhosis or any condition that can possibly affect how the medicine is absorbed into the body.\n* Major surgery scheduled for the duration of the study, affecting walking ability in the opinion of the study doctor.\n* History of heart transplantation, or currently listed for a heart transplant, or current planned use of IV vasodilators and/ or inotropes\n* Prior intolerance/known hypersensitivity to an SGLT2 inhibitor or contraindication to an SGLT2 inhibitor","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"79 Years","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"TREATMENT","enrollment":620,"start":"2025-06-19","pcd":"2028-05-08","upd":"2026-10-23","sponsor":"Pfizer","areas":["other"],"central":["Pfizer CT.gov Call Center · 1-800-718-1021 · ClinicalTrials.gov_Inquiries@pfizer.com"],"sites":[{"f":"National Heart Institute","city":"Beverly Hills","pr":"California","zip":"90211","s":"ANR","lat":34.0736,"lon":-118.4004,"c":""},{"f":"Orange County Research Center","city":"Lake Forest","pr":"California","zip":"92630","s":"ANR","lat":33.647,"lon":-117.6892,"c":""},{"f":"Comprehensive Cardiovascular Care","city":"Santa Maria","pr":"California","zip":"93454","s":"R","lat":34.953,"lon":-120.4357,"c":""},{"f":"FOMAT Medical Research","city":"Santa Maria","pr":"California","zip":"93454","s":"R","lat":34.953,"lon":-120.4357,"c":""},{"f":"Jacksonville Center for Clinical Research","city":"Jacksonville","pr":"Florida","zip":"32216","s":"R","lat":30.3322,"lon":-81.6556,"c":""},{"f":"Infinite Clinical Research","city":"Miami","pr":"Florida","zip":"33133","s":"R","lat":25.7743,"lon":-80.1937,"c":""},{"f":"Flourish Research Acquisition, LLC dba Flourish Research - North Miami","city":"Miami","pr":"Florida","zip":"33138","s":"R","lat":25.7743,"lon":-80.1937,"c":""},{"f":"Amavita Research Services","city":"North Miami Beach","pr":"Florida","zip":"33169","s":"R","lat":25.9332,"lon":-80.1625,"c":""},{"f":"DBC Research USA, Corp","city":"Pembroke Pines","pr":"Florida","zip":"33029","s":"R","lat":26.0032,"lon":-80.2239,"c":""},{"f":"Clinical Site Partners, LLC dba Flourish Research","city":"Winter Park","pr":"Florida","zip":"32789","s":"R","lat":28.6,"lon":-81.3392,"c":""},{"f":"NMH Clinical Research Unit","city":"Chicago","pr":"Illinois","zip":"60611","s":"R","lat":41.85,"lon":-87.65,"c":""},{"f":"Northwestern Memorial HealthCare - Arkes Pavilion","city":"Chicago","pr":"Illinois","zip":"60611","s":"R","lat":41.85,"lon":-87.65,"c":""},{"f":"Northwestern Memorial HealthCare - Feinberg Pavilion","city":"Chicago","pr":"Illinois","zip":"60611","s":"R","lat":41.85,"lon":-87.65,"c":""},{"f":"Northwestern Memorial HealthCare - Galter Pavilion","city":"Chicago","pr":"Illinois","zip":"60611","s":"R","lat":41.85,"